{title: He Goes Before You}
{subtitle: Deuteronomy 31:6–8}
{key: G}
{tempo: 95}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [G] | [G] | [G] | [G] |
| [G] | [G] | [C] | [Em] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Old [G]Moses stood by the Jordan, a hundred and twenty years
[Em]He could not cross the river, but he did not speak with fear
[C]The LORD your God himself will cross over ahead of [Am]you
And Joshua will lead you, [D]as the LORD has said he'd do
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Be [G]strong and courageous
Do not be afraid, [Gmaj7/F#]do [Em]not be terrified
For the LORD your God goes with you [Em7/D]
[C]He will never fail you or forsake [G]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Then he called young Joshua in the sight of all the land
Said [Em]the road ahead is yours now, and the people in your hand
You [C]will bring them to the country that the LORD swore long ago
[Am]To the fathers as their inheri[D]tance, so take it, and go
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [G] | [G] | [Gmaj7/F#] | [Em] |
| [Em7/D] | [C] | [D] | [G] |
| [G] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Em]The LORD himself goes before [C]you; he will be with [Am7]you
He will never fail you or forsake [G]you
Do not be afraid; do not be dismayed
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gmaj7/F#]Be [Em]strong and courageous
[C]He will never fail you or forsake [G]you
{end_of_verse}
